{
  "an3.21:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.21 ",
  "an3.21:0.2": "3. Individuals ",
  "an3.21:0.3": "With Saviṭṭha ",
  "an3.21:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an3.21:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an3.21:1.3": "Then Venerable Saviṭṭha and Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita went up to Venerable Sāriputta, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an3.21:1.4": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, they sat down to one side and Venerable Sāriputta said to Venerable Saviṭṭha, ",
  "an3.21:2.1": "“Reverend Saviṭṭha, these three individuals are found in the world. ",
  "an3.21:2.2": "What three? ",
  "an3.21:2.3": "The direct witness, the one attained to view, and the one freed by faith. ",
  "an3.21:2.4": "These are the three individuals found in the world. ",
  "an3.21:2.5": "Of these three individuals, who do you believe to be the finest?” ",
  "an3.21:3.1": "“Reverend Sāriputta, these three individuals are found in the world. ",
  "an3.21:3.2": "What three? ",
  "an3.21:3.3": "The direct witness, the one attained to view, and the one freed by faith. ",
  "an3.21:3.4": "These are the three individuals found in the world. ",
  "an3.21:3.5": "Of these three individuals, I believe the individual freed by faith to be finest. ",
  "an3.21:3.6": "Why is that? ",
  "an3.21:3.7": "Because this individual’s faculty of faith is extraordinary.” ",
  "an3.21:4.1": "Then Sāriputta said to Mahākoṭṭhita, 